---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I build a sauna myself?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Some buyers assemble listed kits themselves, but foundations, structures, electrical work, wood-burning appliances, chimneys, waterproofing, ventilation, and permits can require qualified professionals. Follow the exact manufacturer instructions and local code rather than a generic online detail."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need a permit to build a sauna?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Requirements vary by address and project. Ask the local building and zoning authorities about the exact structure, foundation, electrical work or fuel-burning appliance, setbacks, inspections, and HOA or design-review rules before ordering."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does it cost to build a sauna?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A dependable estimate requires local quotes and a defined design. Include the kit or materials, heater, freight, permits, foundation, electrical or chimney work, labor, weather protection, access, tax, and contingency."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<Base
  title="How to Build a Sauna: A Safe Planning Sequence for Kits and Custom Builds"
  description="Plan a home sauna build by defining the project, verifying permits, selecting an approved heater, coordinating structure and utilities, and documenting inspections."
  canonical="/guides/how-to-build-a-sauna"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Project planning</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">How to Build a Sauna: A Safe Planning Sequence</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 mb-8">Reviewed August 2026 | Planning guide, not construction drawings</p>

    <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-8">
      <img src="/images/lifestyle/sauna-wood-stove-interior.jpg" alt="Traditional wooden sauna interior with a heater and benches" class="w-full object-cover max-h-80" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
    </div>

    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 text-sm text-stone-700">
      <strong>Scope:</strong> This guide explains project order and decision points. It intentionally does not give universal framing, wiring, chimney, clearance, insulation, vapor-control, or ventilation specifications. Those details must come from the approved plans, product manuals, local code, and qualified trades.
    </div>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="sauna_build_guide_after_scope"
      heading="Organize the project before selecting parts"
      description="Capture the location, heat source, dimensions, budget, timeline, and installation needs before turning general research into quotes."
    />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">1. Define the project before selecting parts</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-stone-700 mb-8">
      <li><strong>Use:</strong> indoor or outdoor, expected users, seated or lying bench space, accessibility, and desired heat experience.</li>
      <li><strong>Format:</strong> listed complete unit, pre-cut kit, panelized kit, site-built room, or detached custom structure.</li>
      <li><strong>Heat source:</strong> electric, wood-fired, or infrared, with the installation and inspection path each requires.</li>
      <li><strong>Site:</strong> survey, setbacks, easements, utilities, drainage, delivery access, and service clearance.</li>
      <li><strong>Budget:</strong> product, freight, tax, permits, foundation, utilities, labor, finish, access, and contingency.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">2. Get project-specific approval requirements</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Contact the zoning and building authorities with the address, dimensions, location, foundation, and heat source. Ask which drawings, product listings, trade permits, and inspections are required. Also check HOA, historic-district, insurance, and utility requirements where applicable.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">Do this before ordering. Permit thresholds and review times are local; generic square-foot or schedule claims are not reliable enough for a purchase decision.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">3. Choose a coherent system</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">The cabin, heater, controls, ventilation, clearances, and electrical or chimney system must be compatible. Prefer a manufacturer-approved package or obtain written approval for the exact combination.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">Select the heater from its rated room-volume method, including the manufacturer's adjustment for glass, masonry, insulation, or other heat-loss surfaces. Do not automatically move to a larger heater.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">4. Coordinate the plans before closing anything</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 mb-8">
      {[
        ["Foundation and structure", "Use plans appropriate to the site, loads, climate, product, and code. Confirm anchoring, drainage, weather protection, and door safety."],
        ["Heat and moisture control", "The wall, ceiling, floor, drainage, finish, and drying strategy must work as an assembly. Follow the approved design rather than combining isolated internet details."],
        ["Electrical", "A qualified electrician should design and permit the circuit, controls, disconnects, conductor routing, lighting, bonding, and inspection scope from the exact equipment documents."],
        ["Wood-fired system", "Use an approved appliance and chimney plan with documented clearances, hearth or ember protection, combustion air, roof penetration, and local fire and insurance review."],
        ["Ventilation", "Follow the sauna and heater manufacturer's required intake and exhaust arrangement. Heater type, controls, mechanical exhaust, and room design can change the correct layout."],
        ["Benches and guards", "Use dimensions and materials that support expected loads, safe movement, heater guarding, cleanability, and the product's required clearances."]
      ].map(([title, body]) => (
        <section class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">{title}</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">{body}</p>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">5. Use hold points</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">A hold point is a moment when work stops until the next condition is documented. Useful hold points include:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-stone-700 mb-8">
      <li>Site and permit approval before purchase or excavation.</li>
      <li>Approved equipment and plans before rough construction.</li>
      <li>Foundation inspection before assembly where required.</li>
      <li>Rough structural, electrical, chimney, or moisture inspection before walls are closed.</li>
      <li>Manufacturer clearance check before heater connection.</li>
      <li>Final inspection and safe startup before normal use.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">6. Document the finished project</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">Keep permits, inspection approvals, as-built photos, manuals, equipment labels, installer contacts, receipts, warranty registration, maintenance instructions, and any approved substitutions. This record helps with service, warranty, insurance, and a future home sale.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Stop and verify before proceeding</h2>
    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8">
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700 text-sm">
        <li>[ ] The location is legally and physically feasible.</li>
        <li>[ ] The cabin and heater combination is approved in writing.</li>
        <li>[ ] The foundation, electrical or chimney, and ventilation plans are coordinated.</li>
        <li>[ ] Required licensed trades and inspections are scheduled.</li>
        <li>[ ] The installed-cost budget includes unknowns and contingency.</li>
        <li>[ ] No concealed work will proceed before its required inspection.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-stone-800 text-white rounded-xl p-6 mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Plan the cost before the build</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-300 mb-4">Use quotes instead of generic averages and keep unknown line items visible.</p>
      <a href="/tools/sauna-cost-calculator/" class="inline-block bg-amber-400 hover:bg-amber-500 text-stone-900 font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-lg">Open the project calculator</a>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-6 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Supporting guides</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/guides/outdoor-sauna-buying-checklist/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Outdoor sauna buying checklist</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-foundation-guide/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Foundation planning guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-electrical-requirements/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Electrical planning guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-door-guide/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Sauna door and egress planning</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/outdoor-sauna-permits/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Permit planning guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-heater-sizing-guide/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Heater sizing guide</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
